DOM + JavaScript CORE CONCEPTS
🔹 1. DOM (Document Object Model)
🔸 Definition

DOM is a tree-like structure created by browser that represents HTML elements as objects, allowing JavaScript to access and manipulate web pages dynamically.

🔸 Key Points
HTML → converted into DOM tree
Each element = node (object)
JS can:
change content
change style
add/remove elements
handle events
🔹 2. append() vs appendChild()
Feature	appendChild()	append()
Add multiple elements	❌	✅
Add text	❌	✅
Return value	returns node	nothing
Flexibility	low	high

👉 append() is modern and flexible.

🔹 3. Event Listener
🔸 Definition

Used to attach an event (click, focus, etc.) to an element.

element.addEventListener("click", function() {
});
🔸 Key Points
Supports multiple events
Better than inline onclick
🔹 4. this in Event Listener
🔸 Rule:
In normal function → this = element
In arrow function → this = outer lexical scope (window)
🔸 MCQ Answer:

👉 B) window / lexical scope

🔹 5. Event Bubbling
🔸 Definition

Event moves from child → parent → root

🔸 Stop propagation
event.stopPropagation();
🔹 6. Event Delegation
🔸 Definition

Using one parent event listener to handle child elements using event.target.

🔸 Advantage
better performance
works for dynamic elements
🔹 7. DOM Selection
Method	Type
getElementsByClassName	live HTMLCollection ❌ static
getElementsByTagName	live HTMLCollection ❌ static
querySelectorAll	static NodeList ✅

👉 Correct answer: querySelectorAll

🔹 8. Create & Append Element
🔸 Task

Create <li> and append to <ul id="myList">

let li = document.createElement("li");
li.textContent = "New Item";

let ul = document.getElementById("myList");
ul.append(li);
🔹 9. Focus Event (Input Highlight)
input.addEventListener("focus", function() {
    this.style.border = "2px solid blue";
});
🔹 10. Destructuring Basics
🔸 Example
const [a, , b] = [1, 2, 3, 4];

👉 b = 3

🔸 Rule
comma skips elements
🔹 11. Spread Operator
[..."hello"]

👉 Result:

["h","e","l","l","o"]
🔹 12. style vs cssText
Feature	style	cssText
Type	individual property	full string
overwrite	no	yes
usage	small changes	bulk styling
🔹 13. getAttribute() vs .href
Feature	getAttribute	.href
value	raw HTML	full URL
resolution	no	yes
🔹 14. Destructuring null/undefined
const { name } = null;

👉 ❌ TypeError

🔸 Fix
const { name } = null || {};
🔹 15. Rest Parameter Rule
const [a, ...b, c] = [1,2,3,4];

👉 ❌ Not allowed

🔸 Rule:
Rest must be last element only
🔹 FINAL QUICK REVISION
DOM = structure of webpage
append = flexible, appendChild = strict
bubbling = child → parent
delegation = parent handles child
querySelectorAll = static NodeList
spread = expand
rest = collect
destructuring = unpack values
arrow function this = lexical scope
cssText = bulk styles
style = individual styles

